-- title:
--   The measure $f(\mathcal A,d)=h(g(\mathcal A,d),\sum d_{s_1},\dots,\sum d_{s_T})$
-- statement:
--   Consider a system whose products are grouped into $T$ categories $S_1,\dots,S_T$ with margins $P_1<\dots<P_T$, so product $i$ in category $t$ has margin $p_i=P_t$. For a function $h$ of a profit value and $T$ totals, the **deterministic measure generated by $h$** is
--
--   $$
--   f(\mathcal A,d)=h\Big(g(\mathcal A,d),\ \sum_{i\in s_1}d_i,\ \dots,\ \sum_{i\in s_T}d_i\Big),
--   $$
--
--   where $g$ is the maximum profit (1) and $\sum_{i\in s_t}d_i$ is the total demand of category $S_t$. When $h$ is strictly increasing in its first argument, its robust measure lies in the class $\Gamma$ of the paper.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Categories are indexed $0,\dots,T-1$ and given by a map from products to categories; the totals are passed to $h$ as one vector.
-- source:
--   Wang, Wang and Zhang, Robust Optimization Approach to Process Flexibility Designs with Contribution Margin Differentials, SSRN 3233721 (version of 2020-05-22), §2.2, display (2), p. 13

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FlexMargin_lpValue

open Finset

namespace FlexMargin

/-- **The deterministic measure `f(𝒜, d) = h(g(𝒜, d), Σd_{s_1}, …, Σd_{s_T})` of (2).**
Wang, Wang and Zhang, *Robust Optimization Approach to Process Flexibility Designs with
Contribution Margin Differentials*, SSRN 3233721 (version of 2020-05-22), §2.2, display (2), p. 13: "f(A,d) = h(g(A,d), Σds1, ..., ΣdsT)", where "For each product
category St, we use the notation Σdst := Σ_{i∈st} di to represent the total demand in product
category St under demand instance d."

The system has plants `Fin m` with capacities `C`, margins `P : Fin T → ℝ` (the paper's
`P_1 < ⋯ < P_T`, 0-based) and the category map `cat : Fin n → Fin T` (product `i` lies in `S_{cat i}`
and has margin `p_i = P (cat i)`). `marginMeasure C P cat h A d` is `h` applied to the maximum profit
`g(A, d)` (`FlexMargin.lpValue`) and to the vector of category demand totals `t ↦ Σ_{cat i = t} d_i`.

**Formalization Note.** Categories are indexed `0, …, T-1`. The class Γ is obtained by
requiring `FlexMargin.IsMonotonicInProfit h`; the same `h` is used for every design. -/
noncomputable def marginMeasure {m n T : ℕ} (C : Fin m → ℝ) (P : Fin T → ℝ)
    (cat : Fin n → Fin T) (h : ℝ → (Fin T → ℝ) → ℝ) (A : Finset (Fin m × Fin n))
    (d : Fin n → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  h (lpValue C (fun i => P (cat i)) A d) (fun t => ∑ i ∈ univ.filter (fun i => cat i = t), d i)

end FlexMargin


